WEBVTT

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.500
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
ima wa ugokenai sore ga sadame dakedo

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:15.580
Right now I can't move... That is my fate, but...

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
akirame wa shinai mou mezameta kara

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.720
I won't give up anymore because I have awakened.

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
moeru tokimeki wa jidai wo utsushi

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:25.890
My burning, throbbing heart reflects the era...

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
iro azayaka ni moesakaru honoo

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.060
It has the color of vividly blazing flames...

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying ima wa mienaku tomo

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.820
Crying, though I can't see it right now...

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching michi shirube wa ukabu

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.350
Searching, a guidepost floats up ahead.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:43.170
I wanna have a pure time!

00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone's a noble mind!

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
soko ni nokotta wakasa toridashi

00:00:48.330 --> 00:00:53.500
I'll take out what remains of my youth there,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:55.980
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.540
beyond the hard times from now!

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
kawaku kuchibiru nureteiru nara

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:06.320
If these dry lips become wet,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
toki wo norikoe atsui jidai e to

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:11.460
Beyond time, towards a passionate era,

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
utsuru darou to shinjiteiru kara

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:16.500
Because I believe it will move...

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:19.060
Believing a sign of Zeta,

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.690
beyond the hard times from now...

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.100
A New Bond

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:09.490
I've never seen this kind of transport
before.

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.770
That makes it forty-five transports.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.240
Bring the boat over here!

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:35.280
Give that to me!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:38.920
Don't touch me!

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.610
Shut up, damn spy!

00:02:41.960 --> 00:02:43.360
Don't move, men!

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:45.590
Or rather, step away from that lady!

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.460
Throw aside your guns and belts!

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:55.400
Run in a straight line!

00:02:57.840 --> 00:02:58.900
Turn, and I'll shoot!

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.200
How do you expect me to run straight
in a jungle?!

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.070
You're allowed to run around the trees!

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:08.610
It's not my intention to make a pass at you.

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:10.880
B-But... who are you?

00:03:11.850 --> 00:03:13.220
My name is Kai Shiden.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.220
As a freelance journalist...

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.590
...I never know when I'll find myself
at the Vatican.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.110
Thanks.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.070
Chicken again?!

00:03:36.140 --> 00:03:38.110
There seems to be a lot of activities
out at Amman.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:41.150
The saying goes, "make haste slowly".

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.150
You're afraid, aren't you?

00:03:42.220 --> 00:03:43.650
Of course I am.

00:03:43.720 --> 00:03:46.780
Petty Officer Masada should have
arrived at Granada by now.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:04:02.430
Granada is unable to grant your requests
for supplies for your ship...

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.470
...because the staff office on Earth
is neglecting us.

00:04:04.670 --> 00:04:08.630
Isn't it because all of Granada
is taking the side of the A.E.U.G.?

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:12.670
If so, we would've destroyed the Alexandria,
rather than allow entry.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:19.480
We want the Alexandria and the Bosnia
to leave in thirty minutes.

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.280
- What about the Sichuan?
- We'll leave it here.

00:04:22.360 --> 00:04:23.380
Understood!

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.960
I heard Anaheim offered to re-supply us.

00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.090
Does that include supplies
for mobile suits as well?

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.260
Yes, sir.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.300
Petty Officer Masada?

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:38.540
Is Kacricon doing all right?

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:41.970
- That's what I'm here to discuss, sir.
- Very well.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:43.240
Haro!

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.680
That word again!

00:04:44.750 --> 00:04:47.180
Okay, then. Your name is Haro!

00:04:47.250 --> 00:04:48.240
Ha ha ha ha ha!

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.280
Amuro! How are you?!

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.080
Amuro?

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:57.750
This chip's ten years old.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.580
Didn't you hear the assembly call?!

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.190
Of course I did!

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:03.590
You're a pilot!

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:05.860
I'm not with the military yet!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:10.330
I hate to say it, but this <i>is</i> the military here!
Come with me!

00:05:16.380 --> 00:05:18.610
That's the forty-eighth today.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:24.350
If you say Jaburo's moved, then where is
the new Earth Federation Forces base?

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:29.280
Even if you found that out,
there's no way of telling your troops...

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.650
...when they could be invading
Jaburo as soon as tomorrow!

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:34.820
Do you plan to return to your capsule
to contact your troops?

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.490
It would take four days by foot.

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.520
Then why not borrow Jaburo's equipment?

00:05:40.130 --> 00:05:41.120
Jaburo's?!

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:43.730
They must have a great
laser communications up-link there.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.860
- But...!
- Not right now.

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.930
We'll try when it gets darker.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.280
So, this ship was built from donations alone.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.620
I'm amazed it got built without
the Earth Federation Forces noticing.

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.150
Those people know too little
about Spacenoids.

00:06:03.220 --> 00:06:05.590
You're aware there was a period
when Europe...

00:06:05.660 --> 00:06:07.630
...didn't take the rising power
of America very seriously.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.190
History has a way of repeating itself.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.520
Hurry! Run!

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.200
You're late!

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:17.640
- Who's that youngster?
- He's a pilot.

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:19.100
- Kamille, is it?
- Yes!

00:06:19.410 --> 00:06:21.470
Hey, little brat! Stop right there!

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:30.880
What did you do that for?!

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:33.890
I'm assuming your tardiness has to do
with that toy. Am I wrong?

00:06:34.460 --> 00:06:35.920
What right do you have to do
what you did?!

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.880
It's not just any toy!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.450
How could you resort to violence
for no reason?!

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:45.670
Stop being such a spoiled brat!

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:51.800
You're no better!

00:06:59.050 --> 00:07:02.710
So you're the Newtype pilot
the Commodore told me about.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:04.150
I'm not what he says!

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:05.850
That's a lie.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:08.320
Despite your words,
I see your arrogance.

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:10.820
It's that carelessness that makes you late
for meetings.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:15.550
Haro is a robot containing a memory chip
with some kind of information!

00:07:15.630 --> 00:07:16.990
I was just trying to check it out.

00:07:17.570 --> 00:07:19.760
You're not an intelligence officer, are you?!

00:07:19.830 --> 00:07:21.860
Then you should do what you're expected
as a pilot first.

00:07:21.940 --> 00:07:24.870
Otherwise, you might find yourself
thrown off of the Argama...

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.370
...and floating in the depths of space!

00:07:27.840 --> 00:07:29.140
But...!

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:32.150
...Haro might've had information
on the White Base.

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:34.740
What use does that have in the battle
we're fighting now?!

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.520
How dare you!

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.310
Will you never stop bickering?!

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.220
Why can't you simply apologize!

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.260
Violence... isn't right.

00:07:54.470 --> 00:07:55.940
So you're up, Newtype?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.700
This happened all because
you talked back to Mr. Wong.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:08.680
I see you're up.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:11.240
- Where to?
- We received orders to head for Granada.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.050
What happened to Haro?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.450
That Haro was a marketed item.

00:08:19.030 --> 00:08:20.990
That was unfair!

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.090
What was?

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:25.960
When I was beaten up for no good reason...

00:08:26.030 --> 00:08:28.830
...all of you just left me behind
without saying a thing!

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:31.600
That's the way the military does things.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:35.630
We were too easy on you while you were on
the Argama. I acknowledge my mistakes.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.810
But that Wong guy isn't a soldier, is he?!

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.500
He's an investor in the A.E.U.G.
He's a very important person.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.550
Kamille!

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:44.380
And that gives him the right to beat me up?

00:08:44.550 --> 00:08:47.020
- Hurry up and get ready!
- I'd rather not!

00:08:51.490 --> 00:08:52.320
Miss Emma...!

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:54.550
The army is a place where many things
are unfair.

00:08:55.500 --> 00:08:58.470
If you don't want to get hit,
eliminate your mistakes.

00:08:59.030 --> 00:09:00.360
I'm not going!

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.330
Then what happens to the Gundam Mk. II?!

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.530
You've got Lieutenant Quattro!

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:08.640
You weren't able to live to this day
on your own strengths alone, you know!

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:11.940
It was because of my strengths that
the Argama was able to survive up till now!

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:17.750
It's that arrogance that'll someday
cost you your life.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:19.840
Mr. Wong hit you because he knew that.

00:09:21.360 --> 00:09:23.790
Arrogance? I only...!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:27.060
Mr. Wong is trying to do something
about the people who cling to Earth...

00:09:27.130 --> 00:09:30.460
...while in the process destroying it.

00:09:30.970 --> 00:09:34.870
With that in mind, he'd like to see people
with your kind of promise survive.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:37.230
I'm nobody special.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.900
I'm an autistic child.

00:09:38.970 --> 00:09:41.940
Don't try to classify adult and child
on your own terms!

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.040
How are you, Kamille?!

00:09:47.110 --> 00:09:48.580
How are you?!

00:09:56.660 --> 00:09:58.280
We're here to test the Hyaku Shiki
and support Granada.

00:09:58.360 --> 00:10:00.330
Be careful, since it's painted brighter now.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:03.050
It's the best way not to be hit
by our own people.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.700
The color of your mobile suits
always becomes popular, Lieutenant.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:09.170
Is Kamille coming?

00:10:09.240 --> 00:10:11.640
He'll come. Lieutenant Emma
will make him.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:13.970
What made Wong so upset at him?

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:16.030
Kamille was being lazy.

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:20.810
There they are.

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:22.350
The Argama?

00:10:22.420 --> 00:10:24.440
Mobile suits.

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.490
What's that? There's a new model.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.250
I don't want to start a mobile suit battle!

00:10:31.330 --> 00:10:33.730
Assuming Petty Officer Masada
has reached Granada...

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:35.730
<i>...how many hours</i>
<i>before reinforcements arrive?</i>

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:37.700
No more than thirty minutes, sir.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:41.600
Let's wait then.

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:45.160
Once we sink the mother ship, the mobile
suits will be easy picking.

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:51.400
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican,
shall we land?

00:10:52.880 --> 00:10:54.370
Let's do that.

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:55.850
Is Jerid ready to take off yet?

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.520
It seems his Hizack is having
some problems.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.380
Will he be ready in time
for Kacricon's operation?

00:11:00.890 --> 00:11:02.050
I'll make him.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:04.920
Lieutenant Jerid has been waiting
for a chance to redeem his honor.

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:07.860
But machines cannot be fixed
with fighting spirit alone.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:10.030
Can you take off?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.090
I'm ready!

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.160
I have a bit of a cold,
but I took medicine to counter it!

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.030
He's also been cleared by the naval doctor.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.570
We'll do an emergency take off.
I've got to catch up.

00:11:19.810 --> 00:11:20.770
Roger!

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.030
Lieutenant Emma, please take care
of the rest.

00:11:25.580 --> 00:11:26.710
Sure thing!

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:29.380
Kamille, catch me!

00:11:33.450 --> 00:11:35.950
<i>I'm opening the spaceport hatch!</i>
<i>I want to minimize the air loss!</i>

00:11:36.020 --> 00:11:37.420
<i>Can you make it?!</i>

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.080
Roger. Panel check, clear.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.390
<i>Preparing catapult!</i>

00:11:40.890 --> 00:11:42.860
Increasing output!

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.170
<i>Opening hatch!</i>

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:52.800
Maximum output!
Adding afterburners!

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:55.770
<i>You don't need to hurry</i> that <i>much!</i>
<i>We'll be okay with our current air level!</i>

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.070
Kamille, let's do it!

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:25.300
<i>Where's Lieutenant Quattro?</i>

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.170
Gundam Mk. II's also launched!

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:36.670
As expected.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.220
- Prepare to take off.
- Yes, sir!

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.290
They say these premises belong to
Anaheim Electronics...

00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:51.130
...but who knows what's being
constructed deep below the surface?

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.890
It's possible that the A.E.U.G. receives its
supplies here.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:57.630
Captain Bask intends to capture this place
without any damage to it!

00:12:57.700 --> 00:13:00.400
I see. Try to gain their gratitude,
rather than attack them.

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.440
Why don't we give them a warning?

00:13:04.710 --> 00:13:06.470
- Hasn't Jerid left yet?!
- No, sir!

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.810
Lieutenant Commander Jamaican.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.910
We will not be conducting
a compulsory investigation of the factory!

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:14.150
That means we will be firing no guns.

00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:17.450
I would like for you to make that point
clear to Chairman Melanie Hue Carbine.

00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:21.460
Of course. And for today,
as a form of salutation to Captain Bask...

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.890
...our chairman has informed us that
we can provide our services without charge.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:26.930
Does your company predict
that the Titans will win?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:29.100
Well, I can't go that far, sir.

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:40.770
I wonder if Lieutenant Quattro knew
it would end up this way.

00:13:40.850 --> 00:13:43.210
I hate this!
He seems to be always testing me.

00:13:51.290 --> 00:13:52.760
What's taking Jerid so long?

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.150
It's Granada!

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:59.200
We'll meet up with those welcoming us.

00:14:06.710 --> 00:14:08.640
Quattro's troops have entered the spaceport!

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.470
We'll commence operations! Got that?!

00:14:10.910 --> 00:14:13.780
- <i>Lieutenant Quattro!</i>
- <i>Give me five minutes!</i>

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.250
What's the plan?

00:14:16.320 --> 00:14:18.580
<i>We're going to capture a Titans ship.</i>

00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:21.450
Why don't we have Granada's troops
do it themselves?

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:24.280
That's why you're looked upon as a child.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:26.920
If we don't make them realize
we are in charge of this operation...

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:29.620
...we won't be able to have
full command of the allies!

00:14:30.930 --> 00:14:32.060
Is that how it works?

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.570
<i>Because there are a lot of people</i>
<i>who want to be in charge.</i>

00:14:34.640 --> 00:14:37.070
<i>Kamille, come with me.</i>
<i>We'll cover for them at the rear.</i>

00:14:37.370 --> 00:14:38.530
Roger!

00:14:46.980 --> 00:14:48.470
Capture a <i>ship?</i>

00:14:48.550 --> 00:14:49.710
<i>A Hizack just came out!</i>

00:14:57.160 --> 00:14:58.780
If you don't move, I won't attack!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:03.290
Okay! We'll take the pilot prisoner!
Apolly!

00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:08.630
Okay! Don't move!

00:15:10.900 --> 00:15:12.900
I suppose we won't fight hand to hand here.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.960
But you'll need to get used to
this kind of combat, too.

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.140
- Don't move!
- Hands up!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:34.020
<i>It won't fire unless you release</i>
<i>the safety valve!</i>

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:39.030
Kitchman!

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:41.090
All we need to do is close off
the spaceport entrance.

00:15:41.170 --> 00:15:42.570
Once we've done that, we'll escape!

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:43.600
<i>Yes, sir!</i>

00:15:44.040 --> 00:15:45.970
Where's Jerid during this
all-important time?

00:15:57.920 --> 00:15:59.390
- What?!
- Enemy attack?

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.060
Lieutenant Quattro! Lieutenant!

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:10.230
Although you wasted bullets
in the process, you did it!

00:16:10.300 --> 00:16:12.160
That's not it! Didn't you feel something?!

00:16:12.570 --> 00:16:14.160
Feel something? Feel what?

00:16:16.370 --> 00:16:17.930
Let's return to Amman!

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:20.300
But our operation isn't complete here yet.

00:16:20.370 --> 00:16:21.530
- But...!
- Such selfish...!

00:16:21.940 --> 00:16:23.570
That's not it!

00:16:27.610 --> 00:16:29.950
- We'll corner them!
- Lieutenant Quattro!

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:32.680
The enemy's gone to the right!
Can they get out that way?!

00:16:33.150 --> 00:16:34.210
It's a dead end.

00:16:34.590 --> 00:16:37.080
<i>He's enjoying people killing each other!</i>

00:16:37.160 --> 00:16:39.460
<i>This isn't war.</i>

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.120
If you don't surrender,
we'll throw in hand grenades!

00:16:46.270 --> 00:16:48.330
Rick Dias! Emma, taking off!

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.700
<i>Hang on a moment to allow time</i>
<i>to start the engine!</i>

00:16:50.770 --> 00:16:51.740
Roger!

00:16:55.480 --> 00:16:56.700
It's fast!

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:04.540
To all GM units! Stay close!
To the spaceport entrance!

00:17:06.650 --> 00:17:08.120
I heard her voice!

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.120
Damn Emma! How dare she fight
as an A.E.U.G. pilot!

00:17:11.490 --> 00:17:13.120
Lieutenant Kacricon!

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:18.960
Spread your legs!
You're hiding a gun there, aren't you?!

00:17:19.030 --> 00:17:20.900
We don't have all day!

00:17:20.970 --> 00:17:21.930
- How are things with you?
- It's alright, sir!

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:23.990
- Take them to the brig!
- Yes, sir!

00:17:24.070 --> 00:17:26.470
It's natural to be scared. You're doing well.

00:17:26.540 --> 00:17:29.740
That's not it. Aren't you concerned
about Amman? About Miss Emma?

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.300
The possibility of Amman
being under attack... I see!

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.580
The guys who attacked you
and Lieutenant Emma!

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:37.840
- I'm returning!
- Thanks!

00:17:39.290 --> 00:17:41.480
Get me Lieutenants
Apolly and Roberto!

00:17:41.690 --> 00:17:44.160
All units, cover the Gundam Mk. II's launch!

00:17:48.230 --> 00:17:49.490
You can't hit me!

00:17:49.560 --> 00:17:50.720
Kitchman!

00:18:01.210 --> 00:18:03.200
That feeling... I'm certain
that it's Miss Emma!

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:13.250
Don't fire the main cannons! If we miss,
we'll damage Amman City!

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:14.840
Open the anti-aircraft fire horizontally!

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.390
Emma! Gotcha!

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.250
You might think you're hiding, but...!

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:47.550
Traitor...!

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.270
Go to hell, traitor!

00:19:23.260 --> 00:19:24.220
An enemy?!

00:19:29.260 --> 00:19:30.750
How dare you bully Miss Emma!

00:19:30.830 --> 00:19:32.920
The Gundam Mk. II!

00:19:46.380 --> 00:19:47.710
You're too slow!

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.050
Dodged it...?!

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:53.450
What?! You mean he...!

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:24.510
Does that guy have eyes
in the back of his head?!

00:20:30.090 --> 00:20:31.580
I was just in time!

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:33.320
Miss Emma!

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:41.890
<i>Kamille!</i>

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.940
<i>Kamille, open your hatch.</i>

00:20:48.780 --> 00:20:49.830
You...!

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:51.170
You came back on your own accord...

00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:53.300
...even though the operation at Granada
is still in progress, didn't you?!

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:55.370
You're wrong!

00:20:55.980 --> 00:20:59.150
It's too soon to have returned after receiving
a distress signal from Amman!

00:20:59.220 --> 00:21:01.690
I sensed that you were
in danger, Miss Emma.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:05.050
- Don't be ridiculous!
- I'm telling the truth!

00:21:05.130 --> 00:21:07.090
You said you needed help, Miss Emma.

00:21:07.790 --> 00:21:09.020
That's what I felt.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:13.190
And when I told Lieutenant Quattro,
he gave me orders to come help you.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:14.360
It's true!

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:16.100
Did I... say that?

00:21:16.770 --> 00:21:18.800
Lieutenant Quattro will verify it for you.

00:21:18.870 --> 00:21:20.600
- What did I say?
- I don't know.

00:21:20.670 --> 00:21:22.900
But I felt that I heard your voice,
Miss Emma.

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:25.710
I could've just had an illusion, though.

00:21:25.780 --> 00:21:27.250
In what way?

00:21:27.310 --> 00:21:29.180
Sounded as if you were screaming,
Miss Emma.

00:21:29.250 --> 00:21:31.270
And the image of you popped into my head.

00:21:32.050 --> 00:21:34.020
Sorry, Kamille.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:35.550
And thank you.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:38.650
If you hadn't come, I would've 
been killed by Kacricon...

00:21:38.730 --> 00:21:40.690
...a comrade from when I was with the Titans.

00:21:42.560 --> 00:21:45.360
Yes. Someone's come to pick us up.

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.600
I understand what you're trying to tell me,
Lieutenant!

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.690
Someone, carry the Mk. II
over to the spaceport!

00:21:49.770 --> 00:21:50.700
Captain!

00:21:50.900 --> 00:21:51.960
I'll do it myself!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.560
I'll have one of the youngsters do it.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:54.940
I'm the youngest one around, right?!

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:58.540
- You want to get hit again?!
- No, sir!

00:22:06.450 --> 00:22:10.050
If you're only helping me on a whim,
I'd prefer that you leave now.

00:22:10.120 --> 00:22:12.110
- Listen up, Miss Reccoa.
- It's <i>Ensign!</i>

00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:16.000
If things with the A.E.U.G. are happening
as quickly as you say they are...

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:17.530
...I'd like to return to space, too.

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:19.620
I understand.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:23.470
However, please refrain from talking to me
in an intimate manner.

00:22:23.700 --> 00:22:25.670
I shall be careful.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.400 --> 00:23:49.330
As he escapes from Granada,
Jamaican stages an attack on Amman.

00:23:49.400 --> 00:23:52.840
There, Kamille learns how
a single mobile suit...

00:23:52.900 --> 00:23:55.390
...is powerless against an all-out attack.

00:23:56.170 --> 00:24:00.110
And when he finally gets away from
the pursuit of Scirocco in his Messala...

00:24:00.180 --> 00:24:03.410
...Kamille sees Fa Yuiry.

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:07.620
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Reunion".

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Next Episode

00:24:07.470 --> 00:24:12.470
Reunion

00:24:07.620 --> 00:24:10.620
You will see the tears of time.
